            "review_text": "HawaiiGuy101\nHonolulu, Hawaii12 contributions\n0\nDon't Eat Here! You'll Get Cheated!\nFeb 2018 • Couples\nThe Chinese restaurant at the hotel ruined our stay there and spoiled what should have been a nice vacation. When we arrived at the restaurant reception desk, we told the young lady that we would be paying \"cash\". In English AND Vietnamese. \nWe ordered lunch and asked for the usual hotel water that is served in the other hotel restaurants and pool area. (You cannot drink tap water in Vietnam and don't even use it for brushing your teeth.)\nWe were told that the Chinese restaurant does not serve the free hotel water but we would have to buy water by the bottle at about $7 US per bottle. We were shocked that they would try to pull such a tactic to squeeze additional money out of the tourists but we had no choice and paid for the water. The water is free everywhere else and in your room as well. \nWhen the bill came, another shock. They wanted us to sign the bill which indicated that we wanted the meal charged to our room. We already had put our money on the table so they were going to double dip a little with cash money and a belief that we wouldn't catch the charge on our checkout statement. They have one type of bill for cash and a different type of bill for meals to be charged to the room. They gave us the bill showing that it would be charged to the room although we had very clearly stated to the receptionist and the waitress that we were paying cash.\nI made quite a scene and the manager of the restaurant didn't even extend an \"I'm sorry\". He was the one who presented the bill and it was obvious that his intention was to cheat us and have us pay twice.\nThe food was average or below which is probably why the restaurant was almost empty. That should have been a warning sign. Taxi's are very cheap and there are lots of restaurants a short $1 US cab ride away. So, skip this place and avoid a headache. \nThe manager of the Chinese restaurant should have been fired. It was so obvious that he was trying to pull a fast one. His actions spoiled what should have been a nice vacation. Shame on the Hotel Nikko for employing such a person of such low moral character. You don't expect to get ripped off at your own hotel. \nI wonder how many people just let them get away with it.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 27, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
